<h2 class="content-wrap-item post__heading post__heading-undefined wp-block-heading pt-default">Key benefits</h2>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="content-wrap-item post__image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img data-ot-ignore decoding="async" width="426" height="426" src="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Recognised_Dark_Blue.png" alt="" class="wp-image-75636" style="object-fit:cover;width:150px;height:150px" srcset="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Recognised_Dark_Blue.png 426w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Recognised_Dark_Blue-300x300.png 300w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Recognised_Dark_Blue-150x150.png 150w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Recognised_Dark_Blue-350x350.png 350w" sizes="(max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Recognized</strong><br>DAX is the defining index for the German equity market, it serves as underlying for financial products (options, futures, ETFs, structured products) and for benchmarking purposes</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="content-wrap-item post__image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img data-ot-ignore decoding="async" width="426" height="426" src="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Transparent_Dark_Blue.png" alt="" class="wp-image-75637" style="object-fit:cover;width:150px;height:150px" srcset="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Transparent_Dark_Blue.png 426w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Transparent_Dark_Blue-300x300.png 300w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Transparent_Dark_Blue-150x150.png 150w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Transparent_Dark_Blue-350x350.png 350w" sizes="(max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Transparent</strong><br>Index calculation and changes to the index composition follow publicly available transparent rules. Please visit the <a href="https://www.stoxx.com/document/Indices/Common/Indexguide/DAX_Equity_Index_Methodology_Guide.pdf">Guide to the DAX Equity Indices</a> for a complete overview</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="content-wrap-item post__image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img data-ot-ignore loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="426" height="427" src="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Diversified_across_sectors_Dark_Blue.png" alt="" class="wp-image-75639" style="object-fit:cover;width:150px;height:150px" srcset="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Diversified_across_sectors_Dark_Blue.png 426w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Diversified_across_sectors_Dark_Blue-300x300.png 300w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Diversified_across_sectors_Dark_Blue-150x150.png 150w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Diversified_across_sectors_Dark_Blue-349x350.png 349w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Diversified across sectors</strong><br>DAX is well diversified across sectors and generally covers over three quarters of the aggregated market cap of companies listed on the Regulated Market of FSE</p>
</div>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="content-wrap-item post__image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img data-ot-ignore loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="426" height="426" src="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Well_Balanced_Dark_Blue.png" alt="" class="wp-image-75640" style="object-fit:cover;width:150px;height:150px" srcset="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Well_Balanced_Dark_Blue.png 426w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Well_Balanced_Dark_Blue-300x300.png 300w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Well_Balanced_Dark_Blue-150x150.png 150w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_Well_Balanced_Dark_Blue-350x350.png 350w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Well balanced</strong><br>Diversification is achieved by incorporating a capping factor of 15% at component level, which ensures that no component can dominate the index</p>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="content-wrap-item post__image aligncenter size-full is-resized"><img data-ot-ignore loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="426" height="426" src="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_High_Quality_Dark_Blue.png" alt="" class="wp-image-75641" style="object-fit:cover;width:150px;height:150px" srcset="https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_High_Quality_Dark_Blue.png 426w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_High_Quality_Dark_Blue-300x300.png 300w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_High_Quality_Dark_Blue-150x150.png 150w, https://stoxx.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/STOXX_Icon_High_Quality_Dark_Blue-350x350.png 350w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 426px) 100vw, 426px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph"><strong>High quality</strong><br>Index components must comply with a set of basic criteria, among which is the requirement for timely publication of financial statements and positive EBITDA for the two most recent fiscal years for new index candidates</p>
</div>
</div>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-text-color has-foam-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-foam-background-color has-background is-style-wide"/>
</div>
</div>



<h2 class="content-wrap-item post__heading post__heading-undefined wp-block-heading pb-sm">Index methodology</h2>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">Index composition is determined on the basis of a clear and publicly available set of rules.</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">The basic criteria for including companies in DAX are: an existing listing on the Regulated Market of the Frankfurt Stock Exchange (FSE), continuous trading on Xetra<sup>®</sup>, minimum free float of 10%, legal headquarters or operating headquarters in Germany, timely publication of audited Annual Financial Report, half-yearly Financial Reports and Quarterly Statements.</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">To be included in DAX, a company that is not an index component yet, must satisfy the following FSE minimum liquidity requirement: minimum order book volume over the last 12 months of 1 bn EUR or turnover rate of 20%. A company that is already an index component must have a FSE minimum order book volume over the last 12 months of at least 0.8 bn EUR or show a turnover rate of 10%. In order to be eligible for DAX, companies that are not components of DAX at the time the ranking list is compiled must show a positive EBITDA for the two most recent fiscal years.</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">The selection of index components is based on free-float market capitalization. The index composition is reviewed quarterly based on the Fast Exist and Fast Entry rules and semi-annually based on the Regular Exit and Regular Entry rules.</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">As of March 18, 2024, the index weighting of an individual share is capped at 15% (previously 10%).</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph wp-block-paragraph">The number of DAX holdings was increased from 30 to 40 effective September 20, 2021.</p>



<p class="content-wrap-item post__paragraph pb-sm wp-block-paragraph">Deutsche Börse Group has been calculating DAX since July 1, 1988. In September 2019, STOXX Ltd. started administering DAX.</p>



